# This file drives GitHub's own "Cite this repository" widget.
# Zenodo ignores it: where a repository contains both CITATION.cff and .zenodo.json,
# Zenodo uses only the .zenodo.json. Keep the two in step by hand.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Police accountability data: United Kingdom, United States and Australia"
message: "If you use this data, please cite it as below, and cite the original publisher of any underlying figure you rely on."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "PoliceComplaint.com"
    website: "https://www.policecomplaint.com/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/copious-git/police-accountability-data"
url: "https://www.policecomplaint.com/data/"
abstract: >-
  Derived, machine-readable datasets on police complaints, stop and search, use of force
  and deaths following police contact for the United Kingdom, the United States and
  Australia. Every figure is computed from official open data by code and carries its
  source, period and denominator. A disparity ratio is a measured difference in outcomes,
  not proof of unlawful conduct; a recorded complaint is an allegation, not a finding.
keywords:
  - police accountability
  - police complaints
  - stop and search
  - deaths in custody
  - open data
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-30"
